{title: 460 - As Water to the Thirsty}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #460 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 460}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]As [F]water to the [Dm]thirsty, as [Gm7]beauty to the [F]eyes,
As [Gm7]strength that follows [Dm]weakness, as [A]truth in[A7]stead of [Dm]lies,
As [Gm7]song[C]time and [Am]spring[Dm]time and [Gm7]summertime to [C]be[C7],
So [Am]is my [Dm]Lord, my [Gm]living [C]Lord so [Bb]is my [Gm7]Lord [C7]to [F]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Like [F]calm [Dm]in [Gm7]place [F]of clamor
[Gm7]Like [Dm]peace [A]that [A7]follows [Dm]pain,
[Gm7][C]Like [Am][Dm]meeting [Gm7][C]after [C7]parting,
[Am][Dm]Like [Gm][C]sunshine [Bb][Gm7]after [C7][F]rain;
[C]Like [F]moonlight and [Dm]starlight and [Gm7]sunlight on [F]the sea,
[Gm7]So [Dm]is [A]my Lord, [A7]my [Dm]living Lord,
[Gm7][C]So [Am]is [Dm]my [Gm7]Lord [C]to [C7]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]As [F]sleep [Dm]that [Gm7]follows [F]fever,
[Gm7]As [Dm]gold [A]instead [A7]of [Dm]grey,
[Gm7][C]As [Am][Dm]freedom [Gm7][C]after [C7]bondage,
[Am][Dm]As [Gm][C]sunrise [Bb]to [Gm7][C7]the [F]day;
[C]As home [F]to the [Dm]trav'ler and [Gm7]all he [F]longs to see,
[Gm7]So [Dm]is my [A]Lord, my [A7]Living Lord [Dm]to me.
{end_of_verse}
